Z||000000||REDHOTT88||11-21-2001||08:05 PM||||I drive my 88 Formula (V6) about an hour and I'm down 1/2 a quart. I check the oil daily<BR>and this still happens.<P>I only notice any smoke from muffler when accelarating hard from first gear. Usually when a little cold.<P>No noticable oil leaks, maybe a couple drops when sits overnight.<P>My dipstick holder has been loose. (Missing the screw that connects to engine.I will replace tommorrow.) But hard to believe that is the culprit.<P>Any thoughts...||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wannabe||11-21-2001||08:16 PM||||Check your oil pan for pinholes. My '88 was blowing oil onto the exhuast just after the cat and burning it off - just a short, barely noticable puff of smoke unless you happened to be looking in the rear view when it would happen. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||REDHOTT88||11-21-2001||08:19 PM||||Will do.. didn't think of that.<BR>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>1988 Red Formula- and she doesn't wear a bra!||||reg||1
